# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This is a proposal, not an available workflow. It describes a shared way to
test file-transfer Python functions in `modernisation-platform-environments`,
instead of creating a separate workflow for each delivery pattern.

## What the workflow should do

When a relevant function, shared code, test or dependency changes, run the
affected unit tests and report the exact revision and any failing suite.
Report a changed function without tests rather than silently skipping it.
Keep a manual rerun option.

The proposed runner would live in `integration-hub`. A cross-repository
trigger needs agreement from the Modernisation Platform team. If that is not
available, a scheduled watcher could check pull-request heads and main.
Before using a watcher, agree how often it runs and where it records tested
revisions so it does not repeat runs or alerts.

## Safety and reporting

Run pull-request code on isolated runners with read-only repository access,
without AWS credentials or Slack secrets. A separate trusted reporting job
would send a concise failure alert to an agreed Slack channel, with a link to
the logs but no file contents, credentials or raw test output.

Notification failures must remain visible. Agree the GitHub App permissions
needed to publish results to the infrastructure pull request before making
the check a merge requirement.

## Before implementing

Agree the trigger, Slack channel and secret owner with the relevant teams.
Use a suite manifest for commands, working directories and pinned development
dependencies, and run every affected suite when shared code changes.

Test a passing run, an intentional failure and its Slack alert, and a manual
rerun. Confirm fork pull requests cannot access Slack or AWS credentials.
This proposal is separate from the existing AWS smoke-test harness, which
checks deployed infrastructure.
